This wasn't supposed to happen.

I had deleted NetHack off my computers to get a break from my obsession, and 
loaded it up again for *moderate* use.  The RNG had other ideas, like making 
booze smoky, putting 2 magic lamps in minetown, and giving my barbarian 2 
sets of wizard bones.

Had most potions IDed early, thanks to a huge liquor store on DL2, so 
alchemy was easy.  When I spotted that smoky potion in the Minetown Deli, I 
knew just what it was.  Uncursed, but one of the magic lamps I bought was 
blessed.  The djinni gave me blessed +2 SDSM.  I already had a cursed CoMR, 
MM, and BoH from Saruman the Wizard.  Altar was cross-aligned, so I went up 
in search of holy water, looting the liquor store on the way.  Finally made 
some at a friendly temple on DL14 and bought 4 pts protection.  After all 
the swimming, blessing, scroll writing, identifying, polypiling, alchemy, 
enchanting, lamp rubbing and booze quaffing, I headed back to clear the 
mines.  Speed boots, CoMR, SDSM, and the blessed fixed +7 Frost Brand made 
it a cakewalk.  Got the wish from the lamp, and didn't want to wait around 
sacrificing for a mere chance at a dominant weapon, especially since Cleaver 
was guaranteed to be first.  I also got an accidental sex change from trying 
on an unknown, uncursed amulet.

I was hoping for the Gnome King's Wine Cellar,  but wasn't THAT lucky.  I 
was happy to get a touchstone and more wizard bones though.  Just below 
Minetown, I did a stupid thing that ended up changing the whole game.  I 
dropped the BoH to get unburdened so I could chase a gray unicorn and was 
too late to stop the gelatinous cube that spawned next to it and ate it. 
AAARGHH.  I stuffed everything into a sack, but was too stressed to climb 
the stairs.  Blessed up the magic lamp from the bones....no wish.  More 
polypiling and alchemy to lighten the load.  3 !oGL and GoP helped. 
Genociding all liches lifted my mood.  I moved the stuff to Minetown and 
brewed up 2 more smoky potions and got a wish!  I replaced my BoH and vowed 
to NEVER TRAVEL BURDENED AGAIN.  I cannot recommend this enough.  My first 
two ascensions were 78K and 85K moves, and this one came in at 58K.  I 
didn't need to carry as much food, making the load even lighter.  Fighting 
was more efficient, Gehennom and the planes are less frustrating.  Its all 
good!

QUESTION:  Strange thing in Minetown.  My large cats had killed the guards, 
so I pickaxed a fountain to swim with scrolls and potions.  The guard's 
shrill whistle went off!  There were no guards, I checked with a potion of 
monster detection.  Is the place wired with alarms and security cameras?

I hit the main dungeon at XL15, AC-23, and 163 HP.  More polypiling yielded 
a pet fire giant and amulet of ESP.  Important, as I didn't get telepathy 
until eating a mind flayer at Fort Ludios.  I gave the fire giant my 
original two-handed sword and we ran a shakedown and protection racket.

