Found the Fort Ludios portal on DL17, and cleared it easily.  Took out 
Croesus by firing 10 worthless pieces of glass across the moat.  Searched 
out and destroyed the land mines and took all the loot.  Found another 
polymorph wand in a chest and zapped the huge pile in the entry door.  Got a 
silver saber,
two-handed sword, a T-shirt, and a bullwhip.  The fire giant had rusted out 
his sword on a black pudding, so I snatched it and gave him the fresh sword. 
All of Croesus' loot bought only my 10th point of protection.  More alchemy, 
enchanting, sacrificing, weight trimming, etc.  I hit the quest portal at 
XL21, AC-29, 207HP.  Thoth Amon was easy.  The fire giant helped out by 
eating troll corpses.  Got a ring of free action from Pelias' chest, and it 
never left my finger.  Say what you will about the Heart of Ahriman, but I 
really like the levitation feature.  Don't have to take off speed boots or 
burn a ring slot or worry about potions expiring over lava or water.

QUESTION:  I spent a lot of time trying to get my fire giant to wield the 
uncursed rustproof +2 Cleaver.  He would pick it up but always drop it, 
preferring to wield Dragonbane.   Is this bad luck or something else?

I killed Medusa by coming up from below.  My fire giant hit a polytrap and 
became a balrog.  Seemed slack at first, but was a real hero at the castle 
til a purple worm ate him.  The WoW was 0:3, I wished for charging scrolls, 
2 magic markers, and a blessed figurine of an Archon.  Used a cursed 
teleport scroll to get back to the altar to prep for Gehennom.  Got another 
djinni from the booze, and wished for a helm of briliiance.  Got a wand of 
death and figurine of a cockatrice from a polypile.  Hit the trapdoor to 
hell with ridiculous overkill, AC-41, twoweaponing +7 Frost Brand and +7 
silver saber, along with a pet Archon.

The Archon lasted 3 levels til he hit a level teleporter.  Couldn't find him 
all the way to the VotD, and he could have been anywhere, so I slogged on 
thru Gehennom alone.  Carried no gold, as I intended to kill all the major 
demons this time instead of paying them off.  They all went down quick 
except Asmodeus, who I surprised from below and he kept teleporting away. 
He didn't summon anyone, though.  I decided to use another wish on a ring of 
conflict, and wore it almost the rest of the game.  Offed Vlad, got the 
candelabraum, and had to dump all my daggers to preserve my unburdened 
conduct.  The only time I was burdened was when I pulled out the pickaxe to 
clear a path between stairs (ran out of digging wands).  I got careless and 
was brainsucked by a MMF at DL40.  Blessed restore ability got my INT back, 
but the ID and level map loss stuck.  The vibrating square was at DL47, 
marked it and went for Rodney.  The ring of conflict helped clear the tower 
zoo, but I took out the disenchanters from distance with wands.  Deathrayed 
Rodney over dry land and took the Book of the Dead.  Cursed teleport to the 
VS and did the invocation.  I got the malignant aura one turn later, and 
found my remove curse scrolls got blanked in a moat accident (have to grease 
that bag!).  Used some holy water instead.  The High Priest of  Moloch was 
tough, and he cursed me some more.  Finally cleared and locked the room, 
took the Amulet, did some BUC testing and alchemy.  Another djinni gave me a 
magic marker, which I used to replenish my remove curse scrolls, and ID some 
things I forgot from the MMF.

The ascension run was even less fun with all the forgotten levels.  The 
Amulet helped with some random clairvoyance, and I used my cursed gain 
levels when I had to.  The mysterious force was very bad.  Rodney stole the 
Amulet and double-troubled at one point, leaving 2 Amulets on his eventual 
corpse.  I knew which one was real, though.  I found my pet Archon in 
Medusa's swamp, but it was stunning and blinding me, so I left it behind.

The planes were a walk in the park.  I was confused, but not stunned by 
casting forgotten spells.  Rodney and the minotaur went down in one deathray 
on Earth, and 4 zaps from the wand of digging got me to the portal.  Invoked 
the Heart and went on.  I was never touched once on Air, all the monsters 
fought each other and I just dodged them.  I took the ring of conflict off 
for Fire to avoid all the messages and make sure I didn't have it on for 
Astral.  The portal was only 20 squares away in the upper right.  My bubble 
on Water floated directly to the portal.

Astral was no such breeze.  First time ever facing Death and first time 
doing the grand tour.  Deathrayed Pestilence on the left, chaotic altar. 
Slogged to the middle, and took Death out in melee, losing 30 max HP.  The 
priests, Archons, and ki-rin were tougher.  I used 4 full heals and 2 
teleport wands before finding the middle altar was lawful.  On the way back 
out I got the sad feeling, my guardian Angel got eaten by a purple worm.  On 
goes the ring of conflict.  I got out what I hoped was an instant rubber 
chicken, but I should have cursed the figurine before applying it, as I 
ended up with a tame cockatrice.  I whistled him around but he didn't stone 
anyone.  Deathrayed Famine, and finally got to the altar. I quaffed my 
potion of hallucination, whistled in my pet, and offered the Amulet to Crom. 
No funny messages.

